repoctl mirror job
==================

The mirror job serves the snapshot "latest" of each set and target on the
HTTP server behind repo.url. It is a bash script with systemd units; repoctl
does not run on the HTTP server. The design is in
docs/design/publish.html#mirror, the runbook in docs/runbooks/mirror-job.html.

Files

  mirror                         the job: /usr/libexec/repoctl-mirror/mirror
  repoctl-mirror.conf            an example of /etc/repoctl-mirror.conf
  repoctl-mirror.service         one run of the job (Type=oneshot)
  repoctl-mirror.timer           starts the service every 5 minutes
  repoctl-mirror-failed.service  OnFailure: runs NOTIFY failed
  repoctl-mirror.sysusers        the system user repoctl-mirror
  repoctl-mirror.tmpfiles        the lock file /run/lock/repoctl-mirror.lock

Needs: bash, coreutils, curl, jq, gnupg2 (gpgv), rpm (rpm, rpmkeys), gzip
(the RepoManifest in the repodata is gzip), util-linux (flock) and systemd.

Install

  install -D -m 0755 mirror /usr/libexec/repoctl-mirror/mirror
  install -D -m 0644 repoctl-mirror.sysusers /usr/lib/sysusers.d/repoctl-mirror.conf
  install -D -m 0644 repoctl-mirror.tmpfiles /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/repoctl-mirror.conf
  install -m 0644 repoctl-mirror*.service repoctl-mirror.timer /etc/systemd/system/
  install -m 0644 repoctl-mirror.conf /etc/repoctl-mirror.conf   # then edit it
  systemd-sysusers; systemd-tmpfiles --create
  systemctl daemon-reload; systemctl enable --now repoctl-mirror.timer

Config

  One mirror line per set and target, with five fields:

    SET TARGET OCI-PACKAGE SERVED-PATH KEYRING

  The keyring is the key file of the release package that the clients of
  the set and target have. Config management puts it at the keyring path in
  the same rollout as these clients. Do not change it by hand to make a
  snapshot pass.

  Settings, one KEY=VALUE per line:

    KEEP_TREES  old trees to keep per line besides the served one (2)
    NOTIFY      a command: "NOTIFY served SET TARGET" after each swap, with
                the annotations of the new latest as JSON on stdin;
                "NOTIFY failed" from repoctl-mirror-failed.service, with the
                last 50 journal lines on stdin (none)
    STATE_DIR   the base of .objects/sha256/ and .trees/ (/var/lib/repoctl-mirror)
    LOCK        the lock of a run (/run/lock/repoctl-mirror.lock)

  A change of the config takes effect at the next run. A line that leaves
  the config loses its symlink, its trees and the objects that no tree uses.

State and the served path

  STATE_DIR/.objects/sha256/HEX        one file per blob, checked by sha256
  STATE_DIR/.trees/SET-TARGET/DIGEST/  one tree of hard links per snapshot
  STATE_DIR/.trees/SET-TARGET/served-path

  The served path of a line is a symlink to the tree that it serves; the job
  replaces it in one rename and never writes into another file there. The
  system user must own the directory of each served path. STATE_DIR must be
  one file system, and the HTTP server must read it and follow the symlink
  (Apache: Options FollowSymLinks; SELinux: the type httpd_sys_content_t on
  STATE_DIR).

  Each served tree holds repoctl-snapshot.json (set, target, digest, publish,
  pulled) for repoctl status, and the heartbeat repoctl-mirror.json (checked,
  result same|swapped|failed, served, latest, behindSince, error).

One run, per line

  1 an anonymous pull token and the manifest of latest; stop when the
    digest is the served digest
  2 the manifest checks: set and target annotations, safe and unique titles
  3 the missing blobs into .objects/sha256/, each checked by sha256
  4 a new tree of hard links
  5 verify with the keyring of the line: gpgv on each repomd.xml.asc (one
    signature), the checksums of repomd.xml, rpmkeys --checksig on each RPM,
    the root key file against the root release RPM, the apiVersion of the
    RepoManifest, the sha256 of each record and the subjects of the records
  6 the revision of each repomd.xml does not go back
  7 repoctl-snapshot.json and the heartbeat into the tree
  8 the swap of the symlink, KEEP_TREES, the objects that no tree uses

  A failed step keeps the old tree, writes the error to the journal and the
  heartbeat, and the job exits with 1 after it tried all lines.

Test hook

  MIRROR_TEST_PLAIN_HTTP=1 talks plain HTTP to the registry. The end-to-end
  test internal/e2e/mirror_test.go uses it for its in-process registry.
  Never set it on an HTTP server.
